-- title:
--   Frames for mathcal I₁^∨⊗mathcal I₂ with prescribed transition function
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a scheme, let $I_1, I_2$ be ideal sheaf data on $X$, let $W_2, W_3$ be open subsets of $X$, and let $a, a' \in \Gamma(X, W_2)$. Assume: for every affine open $U$ of $X$ contained in $W_2$, the ideal $I_2.\mathrm{ideal}\,U$ is the principal ideal generated by the restriction of $a$ to $U$ and this restriction is a non-zero-divisor in $\Gamma(X, U)$; the same holds for $I_1$ with $a'$ in place of $a$; and for every affine open $U$ contained in $W_3$ both $I_1.\mathrm{ideal}\,U$ and $I_2.\mathrm{ideal}\,U$ are the unit ideal. Assume finally that $t \in \Gamma(X, W_2 \sqcap W_3)$ satisfies $t \cdot a|_{W_2 \sqcap W_3} = a'|_{W_2 \sqcap W_3}$. Write $M = I_1.\mathrm{invModule} \otimes I_2.\mathrm{module}$, the tensor product in the monoidal category of sheaves of modules on $X$ of the dual (internal hom into the unit module) of $I_1.\mathrm{module}$ with $I_2.\mathrm{module}$, where $I.\mathrm{module}$ denotes the kernel of the map from the unit module of $X$ to the pushforward along $I.\mathrm{subschemeι}$ of the unit module of the closed subscheme. Then there are sections $p \in \Gamma(M, W_2)$ and $q \in \Gamma(M, W_3)$ such that $p$ is a frame on $W_2$ and $q$ is a frame on $W_3$ — meaning that for every open $W$ contained in $W_2$ (respectively $W_3$) the map $\Gamma(X, W) \to \Gamma(M, W)$, $g \mapsto g \cdot (p|_W)$ (respectively $g \mapsto g \cdot (q|_W)$), is bijective — and such that $q|_{W_2 \sqcap W_3} = t \cdot p|_{W_2 \sqcap W_3}$.
--
--   This is the construction, in the language of frames and transition functions, of the invertible sheaf $\mathcal O(Z_1) \otimes \mathcal O(-Z_2)$ attached to two effective Cartier divisors that are principal on $W_2$ and trivial on $W_3$: the two frames trivialise it on $W_2$ and on $W_3$, and the transition function between them is the ratio $t = a'/a$ of the two generators. It is used for the models of modular curves, where a line bundle is identified with such a tensor product by exhibiting the same pair of frames and the same transition function.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_Scheme_IdealSheafData_exists_isFrameOn_invModule_tensor_module_of_ideal_eq_span.lean

